{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Exempt video-sharing platforms from any proposed social media bans",
        "additional_details": "We call on the government to legally classify video repositories separately from social messaging apps. Proposed social media bans threaten to block sites like YouTube, which lack user-to-user private messaging. For millions of young people\u2014especially neurodivergent individuals\u2014such platforms can be an essential lifeline for education, creative expression, and cognitive regulation. The government must safeguard access by regulating these platforms under a separate framework rather than a blanket ban.",
        "background": "Exempt video-sharing platforms from any proposed social media bans for under-16s.",
